From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Mills <travismills82@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vold: ignore an existing key-upgrade temp directory

Recovery's KeyStorage operation creates /tmp/keymaster_key_blob/ while
handling a key blob. Re-entering that path can legitimately find the
directory already present, which is not an error and should not produce a
spurious PLOG failure.

Keep reporting actual mkdir failures, but accept EEXIST.
---
 KeyStorage.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/KeyStorage.cpp b/KeyStorage.cpp
--- a/KeyStorage.cpp
+++ b/KeyStorage.cpp
@@ -337,7 +337,7 @@ static KeystoreOperation BeginKeystoreOp(Keystore& keystore, const std::string&
     LOG(INFO) << "reading blob_file: " << blob_file;
     std::string blob_dir(kFn_keymaster_key_blob);
     std::string temp_dir = "/tmp/" + blob_dir + "/";
-    if (TEMP_FAILURE_RETRY(mkdir(temp_dir.c_str(), 0700)) == -1) {
+    if (TEMP_FAILURE_RETRY(mkdir(temp_dir.c_str(), 0700)) == -1 && errno != EEXIST) {
         PLOG(ERROR) << "key mkdir " << temp_dir;
     }
     auto upgraded_blob_file = temp_dir + kFn_keymaster_key_blob;
